allegations of employees being bribed. More Investing.com - Amazon (NASDAQ:AMZN) shares struggled midday on a report of employee misconduct, which led to an overall selloff in the tech sector.\nAmazon lost about 2.14% at 12:18 PM ET (16:18 GMT).\nThe company is investigating whether employees sold confidential internal information to third parties to help them boost sales, The Wall Street Journal reported.\n“We hold our employees to a high ethical standard and anyone in violation of our Code faces discipline, including termination and potential legal and criminal penalties,” the company said in a statement to the Journal.\nAmazon was among a host of big-name tech stocks that were struggling in midday trading.\nAmong its other FAANG counterparts, Facebook (NASDAQ:FB) fell about 1.0%, Apple (NASDAQ:AAPL) lost about 1.7%, Netflix (NASDAQ:NFLX) slid about 2.1% and Google parent Alphabet (NASDAQ:GOOGL) was down about 0.9%.\nThe S&P Information Technology sector index fell about 0.8%.\nRelated Articles\nUBS CEO sees no need for dramatic review of targets: Bloomberg TV\nPortugal stocks higher at close of trade; PSI 20 up 0.82%\nDenmark stocks lower at close of trade; OMX Copenhagen 20 down 0.86%", "external_links": ["https://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/_0H_brq5PQYv9R7XY95RAQ--~A/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjtzbT0xO3c9NjUwO2g9NDEw/http://media.zenfs.com/en-US/homerun/investing_com_631/4ae7cd4f0b1b97c1f495947247c7fde6", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/denmark-stocks-lower-at-close-of-trade-omx-copenhagen-20-down-086-1613157?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://www.investing.com/news/technology-news/amazon-investigating-claims-of-employees-leaking-data-for-bribes-1612586?utm_source=yahoo&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=yahoo_finance", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/ubs-ceo-sees-no-need-for-dramatic-review-of-targets-bloomberg-tv-1613178?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=ya